{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"2c439c5c4b44461ba1665d0e637497f6767662df181da4922db0efa2a688dbb0","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM config / Bedrock model integration","key_entities":["REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID","bedrock_model_id","LLMConfig","src/rebar/llm/config.py","src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py","DEFAULT_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID","docs/env-vars.md","cfg.model","providers.py"],"problem_keywords":["config parsing","dead code","unused field","llm bedrock","documentation mismatch"],"propositions":["The bedrock_model_id field on LLMConfig is parsed from REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID environment variable and config file but is never read or used by any code","The actual Bedrock model id is instead carried by cfg.model using a provider-prefixed string format (bedrock:<profile-id>) which is the tested and working path","Setting REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID produces silent failure with no warning, error, or model change since the config field is unused","The unsubmitted change 1043 introduced this dead field and can be cleaned up by deletion before the epic stack lands","Wiring the field would create redundant configuration paths and require precedence rules between two ways to express the same value"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787891023977971001,"uuid":"c5c58f2f-b8de-4656-9091-550871a24e9b"}